from common import U,Q,S,T
UNITS=[
U("A201","Menceritakan kejadian selesai","Memakai Simple Past dengan waktu lampau dan kata kerja teratur/tidak teratur.",
"V2|Regular ed|Irregular verbs|Did not + V1|Did + S + V1|Waktu selesai",
"Simple Past menempatkan kejadian dalam periode lampau yang dianggap selesai: We visited Bandung last week. Kata kerja teratur memakai ed, sedangkan go → went dan buy → bought perlu dipelajari dalam kelompok bermakna. Waktu bisa dinyatakan langsung atau dipahami dari konteks cerita.||Pada negatif dan pertanyaan, did membawa penanda lampau. Karena itu gunakan didn't go dan Did she buy?, bukan didn't went atau Did she bought? Be memiliki pola was/were sendiri. Saat berlatih, ubah satu cerita menjadi positif, negatif, dan pertanyaan agar hubungan bentuk terlihat.",
[("S + V2","She bought a ticket yesterday.","Kejadian lampau selesai."),("S + didn't + V1","We didn't travel by bus.","Negatif."),("Did + S + V1?","Did he buy a ticket?","Pertanyaan.")],
("She didn't went home.","She didn't go home.","Did sudah menandai lampau; kata kerja utama kembali ke V1."),
"Last Saturday, Ana visited her aunt in Bogor. She took the train and bought a snack. Her aunt cooked lunch. They walked in a park, but they didn't visit the museum because it closed early.",
"visit=mengunjungi|take took=mengambil/naik kendaraan|buy bought=membeli|cook=memasak|close=tutup|last=yang lalu",
[Q("Yesterday, she ___ a new notebook.","bought","buy||buys","Buy memiliki V2 bought."),
Q("We didn't ___ the museum.","visit","visited||visiting","Did not diikuti V1."),
Q("___ you take the train yesterday?","Did","Do||Were","Pertanyaan tindakan lampau memakai did."),
Q("V2 dari go adalah …","went","goed||gone","Gone adalah past participle, bukan V2."),
Q("Mengapa mereka tidak mengunjungi museum?","It closed early.","They lost their train.||Her aunt disliked parks.","Alasan disebut sesudah because.","reading"),
S("Ubah ke negatif: He played tennis yesterday.","He didn't play tennis yesterday.||He did not play tennis yesterday.","Hilangkan ed setelah didn't.")],
[T("speaking","Ceritakan perjalanan rekaan kemarin: tiga kegiatan yang dilakukan dan satu yang tidak.","Yesterday, I went to Bogor. I took the train. I visited my aunt. I didn't go to the museum.","V2 untuk positif|V1 setelah didn't|Urutan waktu jelas"),
T("writing","Tulis enam kalimat lampau, memakai go, buy, visit, cook, take, dan not watch.","I went to Bandung. I bought a ticket. I visited my uncle. He cooked lunch. I took some photos. We didn't watch television.","Enam kata kerja|Bentuk tidak teratur tepat|Negatif menggunakan did")],"past",("A108",)),
U("A202","Latar dan kejadian yang menyela","Membedakan keadaan lampau, kegiatan berlangsung, dan kejadian singkat.",
"Was were|Past Continuous|When while|Latar cerita|Kejadian penyela|Urutan kejadian",
"Was/were menyatakan keadaan lampau: I was tired; They were at home. Past Continuous menyoroti kegiatan yang sedang berlangsung pada titik lampau: I was reading at eight. Simple Past menyoroti kejadian sebagai satu peristiwa: The phone rang.||Gabungkan keduanya untuk memberi latar dan kejadian: I was reading when the phone rang. While sering memperkenalkan kegiatan berlangsung, tetapi bukan mesin pemilih tense. Periksa apakah penulis ingin menyoroti proses atau peristiwa selesai. Dua kegiatan berlangsung dapat memakai continuous bersama.",
[("S + was/were + V-ing","They were cooking at six.","Kegiatan sedang berjalan pada waktu lampau."),("process + when + event","I was walking when it started to rain.","Peristiwa terjadi saat proses berlangsung.")],
("They was playing.","They were playing.","They memerlukan were."),
"At seven yesterday evening, Ana was reading while Rafi was cooking. The lights suddenly went out. They were surprised. Rafi stopped cooking and found a torch. Ten minutes later, the lights came back on.",
"rang=berdering lampau|torch=senter|suddenly=tiba-tiba|while=sementara|surprised=terkejut|go out=padam",
[Q("At eight, they ___ studying.","were","was||did","They memakai were."),
Q("I was sleeping when the phone ___.","rang","ring||was ring","Kejadian singkat dinyatakan dengan rang."),
Q("Pilih kalimat keadaan lampau.","She was tired.","She did tired.||She was tire.","Adjective tired dihubungkan dengan was."),
Q("While I was reading, he was cooking menyoroti …","dua proses yang berlangsung bersamaan","dua kejadian yang selalu berulang||rencana masa depan","Dua continuous memberi latar bersamaan.","meaning"),
Q("Apa yang ditemukan Rafi setelah lampu padam?","a torch","a new book||a train ticket","Bacaan menyebut found a torch.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: I ___ watching TV when you called.","was","I berpasangan dengan was.")],
[T("speaking","Ceritakan adegan listrik padam: dua kegiatan yang sedang berlangsung dan dua kejadian sesudahnya.","I was reading while my sister was cooking. The lights went out. We found a torch and sat together.","Latar continuous|Peristiwa simple past|Kronologi dapat diikuti"),
T("writing","Tulis cerita mini enam kalimat dengan satu when dan satu while.","It was Friday evening. I was studying while my brother was drawing. We were quiet. The phone rang when I was checking my notes. I answered it. Our mother asked us to have dinner.","Be lampau tepat|Latar dan peristiwa berbeda|When/while bermakna")],"timeline",("A201",)),
U("A203","Rencana, keputusan, dan prediksi","Memilih bentuk masa depan sesuai alasan pembicara.",
"Going to|Will|Present Continuous untuk arrangements|Prediksi bukti|Keputusan spontan|Ungkapan waktu",
"Be going to sering menunjukkan niat yang sudah ada atau prediksi berdasarkan bukti: Look at those clouds; it is going to rain. Will sering dipakai untuk keputusan saat berbicara, tawaran, janji, dan prediksi menurut pendapat. Makna dapat tumpang tindih; konteks lebih penting daripada satu kata penanda.||Present Continuous juga dapat menyatakan pengaturan yang sudah dibuat: I'm meeting Ana at three. Pastikan lawan bicara tahu waktu masa depannya. Sesudah will gunakan V1. Going to tetap memerlukan am/is/are. Jangan menyebut semua future sebagai satu rumus yang bisa dipertukarkan bebas.",
[("S + be going to + V1","We are going to paint the room.","Niat."),("S + will + V1","I'll carry that bag for you.","Tawaran."),("S + be + V-ing + waktu","I'm meeting Rafi tomorrow.","Pengaturan yang sudah dibuat.")],
("She going to visit us.","She is going to visit us.","Going to membutuhkan bentuk be."),
"Ana has booked a train ticket. She is travelling to Bandung on Friday. She is going to visit her aunt. Rafi sees her heavy bag and says, 'I'll carry it.' Dark clouds appear, so Ana says, 'It's going to rain.'",
"book=memesan|plan=rencana|carry=membawa|cloud=awan|promise=janji|arrangement=pengaturan/janji yang dibuat",
[Q("Bentuk sesudah will adalah …","V1","V2||V-ing tanpa be","Will sebagai modal diikuti bentuk dasar."),
Q("Tawaran spontan saat melihat tas berat …","I'll carry it.","I carried it yesterday.||I am carrying every day.","Will sesuai tawaran saat berbicara.","interaction"),
Q("Pilih bentuk niat yang benar.","She is going to study.","She going to study.||She is going study.","Be + going to + V1."),
Q("I'm meeting Ana tomorrow paling jelas menunjukkan …","pertemuan yang sudah diatur","kebiasaan setiap hari||kejadian kemarin","Waktu tomorrow dan continuous menunjukkan arrangement.","meaning"),
Q("Bukti prediksi hujan dalam bacaan adalah …","dark clouds","a train ticket||a heavy bag","Prediksi didukung awan gelap.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: They ___ going to visit us.","are","They memakai are.")],
[T("speaking","Jelaskan satu niat, satu janji temu, dan satu tawaran. Jelaskan alasan pemilihan bentuknya dalam bahasa Indonesia.","I'm going to learn French. I'm meeting Ana at three. I'll open the door for you.","Tiga fungsi berbeda|Be lengkap|V1 setelah will"),
T("writing","Tulis pesan rencana akhir pekan 50–70 kata, termasuk tawaran kepada teman.","Hi Ana, I'm travelling to Bogor on Saturday morning. I'm going to visit the new library and read there for an hour. I'm meeting Rafi at the station at nine. Would you like to join us? I'll bring an extra umbrella for you. Please tell me by Friday so we can plan the journey together.","50–70 kata|Rencana dan arrangement|Tawaran jelas")],"future",("A202",)),
U("A204","Membandingkan pilihan","Membuat perbandingan dengan alasan dan batas konteks.",
"Comparative er/more|Superlative est/most|Than|As as|Irregular better|Adjective versus adverb",
"Comparative membandingkan dua pihak: cheaper than, more useful than. Superlative memilih ekstrem dalam satu kelompok: the cheapest of the three. Adjective pendek sering memakai er/est; adjective panjang biasanya more/most. Good → better → best perlu dipelajari tersendiri.||As ... as menyatakan kesetaraan pada aspek tertentu: This bag is as heavy as that one. Jangan menggandakan penanda menjadi more cheaper. Sebutkan dimensi perbandingan dan dasarnya; 'lebih baik' tanpa kriteria kurang membantu. Cheap dan useful boleh menghasilkan pilihan berbeda.",
[("A + be + comparative + than + B","Bus A is cheaper than Bus B.","Perbandingan harga."),("the + superlative","This is the most useful book.","Ekstrem dalam kelompok."),("as + adjective + as","This bag is as heavy as yours.","Kesetaraan sifat.")],
("This book is more cheaper.","This book is cheaper.","Cheaper sudah memiliki penanda perbandingan."),
"Bag A costs Rp100,000 and weighs one kilogram. Bag B costs Rp150,000 and weighs half a kilogram. Bag C costs Rp200,000 and weighs two kilograms. Ana wants the lightest bag because she walks to school.",
"cheap=murah|light=ringan|heavy=berat|useful=berguna|weigh=memiliki berat|choice=pilihan",
[Q("Bentuk comparative dari good …","better","gooder||more goodest","Good memiliki bentuk tidak teratur."),
Q("Pilih bentuk yang benar.","more useful","usefullerest||more usefuler","Useful lazim memakai more."),
Q("Kalimat yang benar …","This bag is cheaper than that one.","This bag is more cheaper than that one.||This bag cheaper that one.","Comparative cukup satu penanda."),
Q("Bag mana paling ringan pada bacaan?","Bag B","Bag A||Bag C","Bag B berbobot setengah kilogram.","reading"),
Q("Bag mana paling murah?","Bag A","Bag B||Bag C","Harga terendah Rp100,000.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: This room is as large ___ that one.","as","Kesetaraan memakai as ... as.")],
[T("speaking","Bandingkan dua pilihan transportasi memakai harga, kecepatan, dan kenyamanan. Nyatakan satu pilihan dengan alasan.","The bus is cheaper than the taxi. The taxi is faster, but the bus is comfortable enough for me. I choose the bus because I want to save money.","Tiga kriteria|Bentuk comparative tepat|Kesimpulan didukung alasan"),
T("writing","Tulis rekomendasi tas berdasarkan bacaan tanpa menyatakan satu tas terbaik untuk semua orang.","Bag B is the lightest, so it suits Ana. Bag A is cheaper than Bag B and may suit someone with a smaller budget. Bag C is the heaviest.","Data tepat|Kriteria jelas|Tidak menggeneralisasi pilihan")],"comparison",("A203",)),
U("A205","Pengalaman atau waktu lampau tertentu","Membedakan Present Perfect dasar dari Simple Past.",
"Have has + V3|Pengalaman|Ever never|Already yet|Past Simple kontras|Waktu belum selesai",
"Present Perfect memakai have/has + past participle atau V3 untuk menghubungkan masa lampau dengan sekarang. I've visited Bali menyatakan pengalaman tanpa menetapkan waktu lampau selesai. I visited Bali in 2024 menempatkan kejadian pada waktu tertentu, sehingga memakai Simple Past.||Ever lazim menanyakan pengalaman; never menyatakan belum pernah. Already dan yet membantu menyampaikan status penyelesaian. Jangan menyamakan perfect dengan kata Indonesia 'sudah' pada semua situasi. Have/has berubah sesuai subjek, sementara V3 tetap: she has eaten, they have eaten.",
[("S + have/has + V3","She has finished her work.","Hasil relevan sekarang."),("Have/Has + S + ever + V3?","Have you ever travelled alone?","Pengalaman."),("V2 + waktu selesai","I visited Bali last year.","Peristiwa pada waktu tertentu.")],
("I have visited Bali yesterday.","I visited Bali yesterday.","Yesterday menempatkan peristiwa dalam waktu lampau selesai."),
"Ana has visited Bali twice. She first went there in 2023. This week, she has written a short story about her trip. Rafi hasn't read it yet, but he plans to read it tonight.",
"experience=pengalaman|already=sudah lebih dahulu|yet=belum/sudah dalam konteks|ever=pernah|trip=perjalanan|finish=menyelesaikan",
[Q("She ___ finished her work.","has","have||did has","She memakai has."),
Q("V3 dari eat …","eaten","ate||eated","Ate adalah V2; eaten V3."),
Q("Pilih kalimat dengan waktu yesterday yang tepat.","I visited her yesterday.","I have visited her yesterday.||I has visited her yesterday.","Waktu selesai memakai Simple Past."),
Q("Have you ever travelled alone? menanyakan …","pengalaman sampai sekarang","jadwal besok||jam keberangkatan tertentu","Ever menyoroti pengalaman.","meaning"),
Q("Apakah Rafi sudah membaca cerita Ana?","Not yet.","Yes, in 2023.||Yes, twice.","Hasn't read it yet menyatakan belum.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: They have ___ lunch. (eat → V3)","eaten","Have membutuhkan past participle.")],
[T("speaking","Tanya dua pengalaman tokoh, lalu tanyakan kapan salah satunya terjadi.","Have you ever visited Bali? Yes, I have. When did you go? I went in 2024. Have you ever travelled alone? No, I haven't.","Perfect untuk pengalaman|Past untuk kapan|Jawaban konsisten"),
T("writing","Tulis empat kalimat: dua pengalaman umum, satu waktu spesifik, satu pekerjaan belum selesai.","I have visited Bogor twice. I have travelled by train. I went to Bogor last month. I haven't written my travel story yet.","V3 tepat|Past untuk waktu spesifik|Yet dalam negatif")],"perfect",("A204",)),
U("A206","Kewajiban, larangan, dan saran","Memisahkan mustn't dari don't have to serta memberi saran relevan.",
"Must have to|Mustn't|Don't have to|Should shouldn't|Aturan kontekstual|Bahasa sopan",
"Must dan have to menyatakan kewajiban. Dalam banyak situasi keduanya dapat saling mendekati; materi awal memusatkan pada makna wajib. Mustn't berarti dilarang, sedangkan don't have to berarti tidak wajib. Perbedaannya penting: You mustn't bring food melarang makanan; You don't have to bring food membolehkan datang tanpa makanan.||Should memberi saran, bukan kewajiban mutlak. Sesudah modal must/should gunakan V1. Have to berubah menjadi has to untuk he/she/it. Dalam percakapan, sebut alasan agar saran mudah diterima dan pastikan aturan yang disebut benar-benar diberikan dalam konteks.",
[("S + mustn't + V1","You mustn't touch the equipment.","Larangan."),("S + don't/doesn't have to + V1","You don't have to bring a laptop.","Tidak wajib."),("S + should + V1","You should check the timetable.","Saran.")],
("You don't have to smoke here. (maksudnya dilarang)","You mustn't smoke here.","Tidak wajib dan dilarang berbeda makna."),
"Workshop rules: Visitors must wear a name badge. They mustn't touch the machines. They don't have to bring tools because tools are provided. They should arrive ten minutes early to find their seats.",
"badge=lencana nama|equipment=peralatan|provide=menyediakan|rule=aturan|seat=tempat duduk|arrive=tiba",
[Q("Tidak wajib membawa laptop berarti …","You don't have to bring a laptop.","You mustn't bring a laptop.||You must bring a laptop.","Don't have to menyatakan ketiadaan kewajiban."),
Q("Larangan menyentuh mesin …","You mustn't touch the machines.","You don't have to touch the machines.||You should touch the machines.","Mustn't berarti dilarang."),
Q("She ___ wear a badge.","has to","have to||musts","Have to mengikuti subjek menjadi has to."),
Q("Saran yang benar …","You should check the time.","You should checks the time.||You should to check the time.","Should + V1."),
Q("Mengapa peserta tidak wajib membawa alat?","Tools are provided.","Machines are broken.||The workshop is cancelled.","Alat sudah disediakan.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: You ___ arrive early. (saran, bukan kewajiban; pakai should)","should","Should menandai saran.")],
[T("speaking","Jelaskan satu kewajiban, satu larangan, satu hal opsional, dan satu saran untuk klub.","You must wear a badge. You mustn't run. You don't have to bring paper. You should arrive early.","Empat fungsi dibedakan|Bentuk modal tepat|Alasan atau konteks masuk akal"),
T("writing","Buat panduan empat aturan untuk ruang belajar dengan must, mustn't, don't have to, dan should.","You must keep the room clean. You mustn't eat near the computers. You don't have to bring a pen. You should save your work regularly.","Makna tiap aturan tepat|Kalimat jelas|V1 setelah modal")],"modals",("A205",)),
U("A207","Kata kerja yang diikuti kata kerja","Menggunakan pola to-infinitive dan -ing pada kata kerja umum.",
"Want need plan + to|Enjoy avoid + ing|Like kedua bentuk|Preposition + ing|Purpose to|Chunk learning",
"Dua kata kerja berdekatan tidak selalu berbentuk sama. Want, need, dan plan biasanya diikuti to + V1: I want to learn. Enjoy dan avoid diikuti bentuk ing: I enjoy reading. Belajar kata kerja bersama polanya membantu lebih daripada menghafal daftar terpisah.||To + V1 juga bisa menjelaskan tujuan: I went to the library to study. Sesudah preposisi, bentuk kata kerja biasanya ing: before leaving, interested in learning. Like dapat diikuti reading atau to read; jangan menandai salah satu sebagai salah tanpa konteks. Beberapa perubahan pola mengubah makna dan diperdalam di level berikutnya.",
[("want/plan + to + V1","We plan to visit the library.","Niat."),("enjoy + V-ing","She enjoys drawing.","Kegiatan yang disukai."),("preposition + V-ing","before leaving","Sesudah preposisi.")],
("I enjoy to read.","I enjoy reading.","Enjoy diikuti bentuk ing."),
"Rafi wants to improve his English. He enjoys reading short stories and plans to join a club. Before leaving home, he checks his notebook. He goes to the library to practise with Ana.",
"improve=meningkatkan|enjoy=menikmati|avoid=menghindari|plan=merencanakan|before=sebelum|practise=berlatih",
[Q("I want ___ English.","to learn","learning||learns","Want diikuti to + V1."),
Q("She enjoys ___.","drawing","to draw||draws","Enjoy diikuti ing."),
Q("Before ___, check your bag.","leaving","to leave||left","Before sebagai preposisi diikuti ing."),
Q("To study dalam I went there to study menunjukkan …","tujuan","peristiwa yang sudah selesai||pemilik benda","To-infinitive dapat menjelaskan tujuan.","meaning"),
Q("Apa yang Rafi rencanakan?","to join a club","to leave his notebook||to avoid all books","Plans to join a club disebut jelas.","reading"),
S("Lengkapi: We plan ___ visit Ana.","to","Plan diikuti to-infinitive.")],
[T("speaking","Ceritakan rencana belajar dengan want, plan, enjoy, dan before.","I want to speak clearly. I plan to join a club. I enjoy reading stories. Before speaking, I check my ideas.","Empat pola|To dan ing tepat|Tujuan belajar jelas"),
T("writing","Tulis lima kalimat rencana akhir pekan, termasuk satu tujuan dengan to.","I want to visit the library. I plan to go on Saturday. I enjoy reading stories. Before leaving, I pack my notebook. I go there to study.","Lima kalimat terhubung|Pola verb benar|Purpose to digunakan")],"verb-patterns",("A206",)),
U("A208","Cerita dan pesan yang runtut","Menghasilkan narasi pendek dengan urutan, alasan, dan rujukan jelas.",
"First then finally|Past narrative|Because so|Pronoun reference|Pesan meminta informasi|Revisi kalimat",
"Narasi yang mudah diikuti memiliki orientasi, rangkaian kejadian, dan hasil. First, then, after that, finally dapat membantu, tetapi hubungan waktu juga bisa terlihat dari isi. Jangan menambahkan penghubung pada setiap kalimat secara mekanis.||Because memperkenalkan alasan; so memperkenalkan akibat. Dalam pola yang diajarkan di sini, pilih salah satu: I stayed home because it rained; It rained, so I stayed home. Saat merevisi, periksa apakah pembaca dapat mengetahui siapa pelaku setiap he/she/they, kapan kejadian terjadi, dan mengapa hasilnya masuk akal.",
[("event + because + reason","We left because it was late.","Alasan."),("reason + so + result","It was late, so we left.","Akibat.")],
("Because it rained, so we stayed home.","Because it rained, we stayed home.","Satu hubungan sebab tidak perlu ditandai dua kali dengan pola ini."),
"Yesterday, Ana planned to visit a museum. First, she checked the opening time. Then she took a bus with Rafi. The bus arrived late, so they had only one hour inside. They enjoyed the paintings. Finally, they wrote to the museum to ask about a return visit.",
"opening time=jam buka|painting=lukisan|return visit=kunjungan kembali|finally=akhirnya|result=hasil|reason=alasan",
[Q("It rained, ___ we stayed home.","so","because||although because","Klausa kedua adalah akibat."),
Q("We stayed home ___ it rained.","because","so||then because so","Klausa kedua memberi alasan."),
Q("Mengapa waktu di museum hanya satu jam?","The bus arrived late.","The museum had no paintings.||They forgot the opening time.","Hubungan sebab dinyatakan dalam bacaan.","reading"),
Q("Yang dilakukan Ana sebelum naik bus …","checked the opening time","wrote a return request||bought a painting","First menandai langkah awal.","reading"),
Q("Revisi yang paling jelas untuk Rafi met Bima. He was late, jika Bima terlambat …","Rafi met Bima. Bima was late.","Rafi met Bima. They he was late.||Rafi met Bima. It was him his.","Mengulang nama menghilangkan rujukan ambigu.","writing"),
S("Lengkapi penanda akhir: First, we planned. Then, we travelled. ___, we went home.","Finally","Finally dapat menandai tahap terakhir.","writing")],
[T("speaking","Ceritakan perjalanan rekaan 60–90 detik dengan tujuan, satu masalah, solusi, dan hasil.","We wanted to visit a museum. Our bus arrived late, so we changed our plan. We saw one exhibition and asked about a return visit. We enjoyed the trip.","Empat unsur cerita|Waktu lampau konsisten|Sebab-akibat jelas"),
T("writing","Tulis narasi 80–100 kata dan dua pertanyaan informasi untuk penyelenggara kegiatan.","Last Saturday, our class visited a small museum in Bogor. We wanted to learn about local transport. First, we checked the timetable and met at school. Our bus arrived late, so we had less time than expected. A guide helped us choose one exhibition. We took notes and asked questions about the old trains. Before leaving, we thanked the guide. We would like to return next month with more time. What time does the museum open on Sunday? Do students have to book tickets in advance?","80–100 kata|Masalah dan hasil|Dua pertanyaan akurat")],"paragraph",("A207",))
]
